  "body": "## What happens\n\nPR #4499 (#4417) makes the Fanuc and Doosan DNM posts write the joint angles of an A-outer tilt chain (A carries B), solved from the stream pose. The machine travel check (`judge.rs::pose_problems`) judges the same joint angles.\n\nThe simulation does not follow yet. `crates/sim/src/sim.rs` (about line 636, `move_legs` rotary leg times) and the sim rotary field read the stream A/B letters, not the joint angles. So on a tilt-head machine where A carries B:\n- the time estimate of a rotary move uses the wrong angle change;\n- the rotary band in the simulation shows the stream letters, not the angles that the machine turns to.\n\nThe posted G-code and the travel check are correct (#4499). This issue is about the display and the time estimate only.\n\n## Evidence\n\nFound by the independent pre-review of PR #4499 at head `c91e47da3`.\n\n## Done means\n\n- The simulation uses the same joint-angle rule as the post and the check (`crates/post/src/machine/tilt_chain.rs::joint_angles`, or a shared function), so the rotary leg time and the rotary band show the joint angles.\n- A test on `tilthead.mch`: a pose with A and B both turning shows the joint angles in the rotary band, and the leg time follows the joint-angle change.\n- No change to posted G-code.\n",
